<title>UK: BA October passenger traffic up 6.5 pct.</title>
<headline>BA October passenger traffic up 6.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Monday paying passenger traffic in October rose 6.5 percent but capacity rose 7.9 percent to give an overall load factor of 75.3 percent -- down one percentage point on last year, which was at record levels.</p>
<p>BA said premium traffic was up by 4.6 percent on a year ago while main cabin traffic rose by 6.9 percent, the highest year on year rise so far this financial year.  </p>
<p>British Airways operating statistics OCTOBER 1996 vs 1995 Passengers carried (millions)</p>
<p>UK/Europe	  - 1.988 vs 1.925 (up 3.2 pct)</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 1.030 vs 0.956 (up 7.7 pct)</p>
<p>Total		- 3.017 vs 2.881 (up 4.7 pct)</p>
<p>Traffic (millions Revenue Passenger Kilometres)</p>
<p>UK/Europe	  - 1,718 vs 1,626 (up 5.6 pct)</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 7,421 vs 6,956 (up 6.7 pct)</p>
<p>Total		- 9,138 vs 8,582 (up 6.5 pct)</p>
<p>Capacity (millions Available Seat Kilometres)</p>
<p>UK/Europe	  - 2,439 vs 2,268 (up 7.6 pct)</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 9,701 vs 8,987 (up 8.0 pct)</p>
<p>Total		- 12,140 vs 11,254 (up 7.9 pct)</p>
<p>Passenger load factor</p>
<p>UK/Europe	  - 70.4 percent vs 71.7 percent</p>
<p>Intercontinental - 76.5 percent vs 77.4 percent</p>
<p>Total		- 75.3 percent vs 76.3 percent</p>
<p>Cargo		- 333 million vs 310 million Cargo Tonne Kilometres</p>
</text>
